&lt;h2 id="garden"&gt;Garden&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial restaurant garden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="keywords"&gt;Keywords&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/search/?q=tables"&gt;tables (support furniture)&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a class="id" target="_blank" href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300039548" title="Art and Architecture Thesaurus (Getty)"&gt;AAT:300039548&lt;/a&gt;)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This garden restaurant was strategically located across from the Palaestra. This garden occupied most of the southern part of this &lt;em&gt;insula&lt;/em&gt; and had a masonry &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300004359" target="_blank"&gt;triclinium&lt;/a&gt; (l. medius, 4.90 m; l. imus and summus 4.50m), as well as a round table (1.00 m in diameter) and a square table (0.90m x 0.90m).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="dates"&gt;Dates&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1951-1953.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="bibliography"&gt;Bibliography&lt;/h2&gt;
